entry.summary:
So I'm participating in the HNG13 internship program and our stage 0 task was to build a simple API to Return your Profile and a Random Cat Fact. I’ve been learning Go (Golang) for a while now and wanted to build it with that and here's how it went. In this post, I’ll walk you through how I built this tiny Go + Gin API. 🔧 Stack Go (Golang) Gin - HTTP web framework catfact.ninja API - Free API to fetch random cat facts 🛠️ What the API Does When you hit the endpoint /me, the API returns: My name, email, and stack The current timestamp (UTC) A random cat fact 🐱 Here’s an example response: { "status": "success", 🚀 Setting Up the Controller The core logic lives inside the controller. Here's the full code: package controllers import ( "github.com/gin-gonic/gin"
